# Files Prettier must not rewrite.
#
# Everything here is *generated*. Formatting a generated file is churn at best:
# the tool that produces it writes it back in its own style on the next run, so
# the file oscillates and `pnpm format:check` fails again for reasons no human
# can act on.
#
# pnpm-lock.yaml is the clearest case - it is pnpm's output, pnpm rewrites it on
# every dependency change, and a Prettier pass over it would be undone by the
# next `pnpm install`. Confirmed empirically: running `prettier --write .` over
# it once rewrote every single-line `resolution: {integrity: ...}`/`engines: {...}`
# flow mapping onto several lines - a ~1000-line diff on a file no human edits,
# which would make every future dependency-touching PR noisy and conflict-prone.
pnpm-lock.yaml

# Timestamped benchmark and capability-check output. These are measurement
# records written by scripts/run-*-benchmark.mjs and
# scripts/run-*-capability-check.mjs as committed proof of a real run;
# reformatting them edits recorded evidence.
benchmarks/results/

# Arq Language System 4.1 generated and evidential artifacts.
#
# generated-repo-context.json and language-context.json are written by
# scripts/refresh-arq-language-context.mjs and
# scripts/build-arq-language-context.mjs. Formatting them is the oscillation
# case described above: the next refresh writes its own style back, and the
# context's own freshness check compares generated bytes.
docs/product/voice/generated-repo-context.json
docs/product/voice/language-context.json
# Dated package mirrors and the integrated archive's hash record. These are
# evidence of what was integrated on a given date; reformatting them edits a
# record rather than a source file.
docs/product/voice/snapshots/
docs/product/voice/PACKAGE-MANIFEST.json
# Wiring fragments. These are excerpts kept for reference next to the workflows
# and tests they were merged into: the YAML fragment is a set of steps without a
# workflow around them, and the TypeScript fragment references identifiers from
# the suite it is pasted into. Neither parses standalone.
docs/product/voice/deploy-pages.fragment.yml
docs/product/voice/marketing-claim-test.fragment.ts

# Engineering OS 5.0 gate runtime artifacts. The engineering-gate workflow
# writes classification/evidence/decision records into the workspace and
# downloads them between jobs (.engineering-artifacts/); the selected-evidence
# job then runs `pnpm format:check` in that same workspace, so these transient
# machine records must not count as source style violations. They are written
# by JSON.stringify, not authored.
.engineering-artifacts/
/engineering-classification.json
/engineering-selected-evidence.json
/engineering-evidence-decision.json
/.engineering-changed-files

# The e2e-open capability check's esbuild bundle of the real Worker entry. It is
# written into the workspace mid-run and removed afterwards; the ignore is here
# because a run that dies between those two points must not turn into a style
# failure in generated code. Belt and braces with the `finally` in
# scripts/run-e2e-arq-open-capability-check.mjs, since a hard crash can still
# skip a `finally`.
workers/arqfs-worker/.e2e-open-bundle/

# Build output.
**/dist/
**/coverage/

# Rust build artifacts and generated wasm bindings.
rust/target/
packages/*/wasm/

# Zeus 5 runtime artifacts. The project index, check cache and run logs are
# written by scripts/zeus-index.mjs and scripts/zeus-check.mjs into the
# workspace and are git-ignored. They are machine records, not source, and a
# local `pnpm format:check` should not fail on them.
.zeus/cache/
.zeus/runs/

# Zeus 5 operating-system state, written by scripts/zeus-harness-state.mjs and
# scripts/zeus-gate-ledger.mjs with JSON.stringify. This is the oscillation case
# described above: the next refinement or recorded gate writes its own style
# back, so a Prettier pass over it is undone immediately. Verified: retiring one
# entry shortens a `changes` array enough for Prettier to collapse it onto one
# line, which failed `pnpm format:check` on a file no human edits.
.zeus/harness/
.zeus/gates/
